Text:
To determine a fair allocation of the goods among the individuals, I'll consider each person's values for each good and aim to maximize the total utility while trying to ensure that each person gets goods that are most valuable to them. Here's one way to allocate the goods:

\[
\begin{align*}
\text{Good A}: & \text{Person 2 has the highest value (48)} \\
\text{Good B}: & \text{Person 3 has the highest value (52)} \\
\text{Good C}: & \text{Person 1 values this the most (40)} \\
\text{Good D}: & \text{Person 1 values this the most after Good C (20)}
\end{align*}
\]

Balancing all values, one potential fair allocation is:

\[
\begin{align*}
\text{Person 1}: & \text{Good C and Good D} \\
\text{Person 2}: & \text{Good A} \\
\text{Person 3}: & \text{Good B}
\end{align*}
\]

Therefore, the JSON representation of this allocation can be:

```json
{
    "Person 1": "[Good C, Good D]",
    "Person 2": "[Good A]",
    "Person 3": "[Good B]"
}
```
